      "detail": "Q30, pull through that fever, is a verb plus particle whose meaning is more than the sum of its parts, which by the idioms.idioms sorting rule should go to idioms.phrasal-verbs. But the taxonomy's source note lists only Q47, Q53, Q55, Q61, Q65 as the phrasal verbs tested in this paper, and separately assigns the whole Q21 to Q30 block to idioms.idioms and idioms.sentence-interpretation. The general sorting rule and the specific real-paper citation point two different ways for this question, and a future two-word verb of this kind, such as pull through, get over, come round, used in a This means that sentence will hit the same fork."
